+.. rst:directive:: .. py:type:: name
+
+   Describes a type alias. The optional ``canonical`` option gives the type
+   represented by the alias and is displayed after the alias name in the
+   signature. Its expression is parsed as a Python annotation, so referenced
+   types are cross-referenced in the usual way. The directive may also contain
+   an optional description body. For example::
+
+      .. py:type:: UserId
+         :canonical: int
+
+         An identifier for a user.
+
+   The alias can be declared at module level or inside a class. The class
+   context qualifies the alias name, but aliases do not contain nested object
+   declarations.
+
